  <section class="sec">
    <h2>What a Mac gives you today.</h2>
    <p>Either the raw file in a text editor, or an app that would like you to make an account, create a library, and import your files before it shows you anything.</p>
    <div class="today">
      <figure>
        <div class="win">
          <div class="win__bar"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span>Field notes.md</span></div>
          <div class="wall"># Field notes, September

**Three days in the Lakes, one notebook, no signal.**

&gt; The plan was Helvellyn on Saturday and a long, flat Sunday. The weather had other plans, and so did the pen.

I keep these in plain Markdown so they open anywhere, and so that in ten years they will still open. This one has a table, a list of things to do, a footnote and a photograph, which is about as much structure as a walk deserves.

## Saturday

Up at six. Frost on the tent, the first of the year, and the tarn completely still. Striding Edge by nine; the ridge was empty apart from two runners and a dog with better balance than either of us.

Lunch at Red Tarn. Too cold to sit for long, so we didn't.

| Leg | Miles | Ascent | Weather |
|:---|---:|---:|:---|
| Glenridding to Red Tarn | 3.1 | 1,600 ft | Frost, then sun |
| Striding Edge to the summit | 1.4 | 900 ft | Wind from the west |
| Swirral Edge and back down | 3.6 | 0 ft | Clear, cold |

![Red Tarn at seven in the morning, still enough to hold the ridge upside down.](images/tarn.jpg)</div>
